* German Trio preamp, stage 4 of 5 (Crunch and Lead): V3A, the V3B cathode follower, 220n, and the tone controls and VOLUME of the channel.
* V2B's plate arrives through the link source VV3; its coupling network (22n, 332k, 221k) is repeated.
*
* The two channels have the same tone stack with different resistors (the 100k from the stack's output to the volume pot is 221k in Lead
* and the one from the HIGH wiper is 332k instead of 100k); one set of pots serves both, the switch resistors SW_E* pick the values.
* Stack: input -> MID (100k) -> 100k to the LOW pot, 100p + 470k and the bass caps (1n) -> HIGH (1M with 2.2n) -> the two resistors -> VOLUME 1M.
* V3A 221k plate load, 1k82 + 1u; V3B is a follower (plate on the rail, 100k cathode resistor) at 200 V.
* The volume's wiper (vw) goes through the contact (CR or LE) to V4A in stage 5, with its loads repeated.

V VRAIL x 100 380
V VX3 x3 50 392
C C33u x3 0 33u
S VV3 p2b 1 0
C C22b p2b n2 22n
R R332 n2 0 332k
R R221b n2 g3a 221k
T V3A g3a p3a k3a 12AX7
R R3A x3 p3a 221k
R RK3A k3a 0 1k82
C CK3A k3a 0 1u
T V3B p3a x3 k3b 12AX7
R RK3B k3b 0 100k
C C220 k3b e0 220n
R R1ME e0 0 1M

* Tone stack (same topology in both channels).
C CE10a e0 f 10n
R RE10k f 0 10k
C CE10b f pm 10n
R VRM_T e0 tn 1
R VRM_B tn pm 1
C CE100p tn tt 100p
R RE470 tt c 470k
R RE100 tn lb 100k
R VRL_T lb c 1
R VRL_B c rr 1
C CE1a c lb 1n
C CE1b c rr 1n
R RE10b rr 0 10k
R VRH_T c hw 1
R VRH_B hw hr 1
C CE22n hr 0 2.2n
R SW_ECR1 c a1 1
R RE100a a1 vt 100k
R SW_ELE1 c b1 1e12
R RE221 b1 vt 221k
R SW_ECR2 hw a2 1
R RE100b a2 vt 100k
R SW_ELE2 hw b2 1e12
R RE332 b2 vt 332k
R VRV_T vt vw 1
R VRV_B vw 0 1
R R1MV vw 0 1M
C C100n vw gl 100n
R R1MG gl 0 1M
